ineal tumors, are rare tumors that can affect the pineal gland. These tumors are classified into several types, including germ cell tumors and others.", "HISTIOCITOSIS X:Histiocytosis X is a rare disease characterized by the proliferation of histiocytes, which can affect various organs including the pituitary gland.", "ENFERMEDAD DE ERDHEIM-CHESTER:Erdheim-Chester disease is a rare form of non-Langerhans histiocytosis that can cause systemic symptoms and affect the pituitary gland.", "GLANDULA PINEAL:The pineal gland is a small endocrine gland in the brain that produces melatonin and can be affected by tumors.", "LOPES MB:Lopes MB is an author who co-wrote the overview of the 2017 WHO Classification of Pituitary Tumors.", "ANDÚJAR P:Andújar P is an author who wrote about the pathology of the hypothalamic-pituitary axis and pineal tumors.", "JACOBSEN E:Jacobsen E is an author who has written about Erdheim-Chester disease.", "METE O:", "GLÁNDULA PINEAL:La glándula pineal es una pequeña glándula endocrina en el cerebro que produce melatonina y está relacionada con varios tumores, como los germinomas.", "GERMINOMAS:Los germinomas son un tipo de tumor que se origina en las células germinales y son los más frecuentes en la glándula pineal.", "SÍNDROME DE PARINAUD:El síndrome de Parinaud es un conjunto de síntomas neurológicos que puede presentarse en pacientes con tumores en la región pineal, así como en aquellos con tumores en la región selar, como los adenomas hipofisarios. Uno de los síntomas característicos del síndrome de Parinaud es la parálisis de la mirada superior, que puede afectar la capacidad del paciente para mover los ojos hacia arriba. Este síndrome es relevante en el contexto de tumores que afectan estas áreas del cerebro, indicando la necesidad de una evaluación neurológica en pacientes con tales condiciones.", "HCG:Human Chorionic Gonadotropin (HCG) is a hormone produced during pregnancy that plays a crucial role in stimulating thyroid hormone production and influencing TSH (Thyroid Stimulating Hormone) levels. In addition to its role in pregnancy, HCG is utilized in medical treatments to stimulate testosterone production in males. It is important to note that HCG can also be produced by tumors of the pineal gland, which may lead to effects on the production of both testosterone and estrogens. Furthermore, HCG can cause secondary hyperthyroidism by binding to the TSH receptor. Overall, HCG is a multifaceted hormone with significant implications in both reproductive health and endocrine function.", "AIP:AIP is a tumor suppressor gene that plays a significant role in the development of pituitary adenomas. It is particularly associated with isolated familial pituitary adenomas (FIPA). Additionally, the AIP gene may also be linked to the formation of craniopharyngiomas.", "MEN1:MEN1, or Multiple Endocrine Neoplasia Type 1, is a hereditary genetic syndrome that significantly increases the risk of developing multiple endocrine tumors. This condition is characterized by the formation of tumors in various endocrine glands, including the parathyroid glands, anterior pituitary, and pancreatic islet cells. Among the tumors associated with MEN1 are gastrinomas, which produce the gastrin hormone, and insulinomas, which are linked to a prevalence of 6-10% in cases of insulinoma. MEN1 is recognized as a tumor suppressor gene and is a focus of clinical guidelines and treatment strategies aimed at managing the associated risks of both endocrine and non-endocrine tumors. Overall, MEN1 is a complex syndrome that necessitates careful monitoring and management due to its multifaceted impact on endocrine health.", "PRKARIA:PRKARIA es un gen que actúa como supresor tumoral y está implicado en la patogenia de los adenomas hipofisarios."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}